=== REPORTED (not graded) ===
  R1: BK's Solar-System argument (flow above a critical velocity near the Sun, condensate loses coherence) uses the same criterion G0 computes: once E_q > mu_eff the pair band at twist q lies above the chemical potential (KA8) and no condensate exists at any coupling. That is the gradient-dominated condition itself, so it holds wherever BK's MOND regime is used, not only near the Sun.
  R4: kappa: a0' = alpha^3 Lambda^2/(8 pi M_Pl) with Lambda_eff = nu_s/(32 pi m_f) (tangle) or c_6 (k^6): every branch carries a free dimensionful input, not tied to rho_DE. The 5.41 is untouched.
  R5 strong pairing (BEC side, E_b = 10): d ln P/d ln mu_eff = D2 1.994, D5 1.902 (a Bose gas of pairs, not the Fermi sea's 3/2)

